Subject: [PATCH] qmutex: FutexAlwaysAvailable must honour QT_LINUXBASE

qfutex_p.h selects the Linux futex backend with

    #elif defined(Q_OS_LINUX) && !defined(QT_LINUXBASE)

but QBasicMutex::FutexAlwaysAvailable is true for Q_OS_LINUX alone. A
QT_LINUXBASE build therefore gets the dummy futex, does not define
QT_ALWAYS_USE_FUTEX, and stops in qmutex.cpp at

    static_assert(!FutexAlwaysAvailable, "mismatch with QT_ALWAYS_USE_FUTEX");

The two conditions describe the same decision and must be the same.

--- a/src/corelib/thread/qmutex.h
+++ b/src/corelib/thread/qmutex.h
@@ -25,7 +25,7 @@
     Q_DISABLE_COPY_MOVE(QBasicMutex)
 protected:
     static constexpr bool FutexAlwaysAvailable =
-#if defined(Q_OS_FREEBSD) || defined(Q_OS_LINUX) || defined(Q_OS_WIN) // these platforms use futex
+#if defined(Q_OS_FREEBSD) || (defined(Q_OS_LINUX) && !defined(QT_LINUXBASE)) || defined(Q_OS_WIN) // these platforms use futex
             true
 #else
             false
